                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course is designed for clinical medicine students and consists of 32 class hours. The content covers basic knowledge and cutting-edge information in sports medicine, such as biomechanics, sports rehabilitation, sports physiology, the principles of arthroscopic technology, common sports injuries of the shoulder, knee, hip and ankle joints, medical support for high-level athletes, regenerative medicine and artificial intelligence, etc. Through learning this course, students can master the basic concepts of sports medicine, acquire diagnostic methods and handling principles for common sports injuries, be familiar with the formulation of exercise prescriptions for common diseases, and understand the movement characteristics of high-level athletes. During the teaching process of this course, by analyzing real cases of athletes, it strengthens humanistic medical education and medical ethics education, promotes the "truth", "goodness" and "beauty" of the medical profession spirit, and cultivates innovative and outstanding medical talents with a strong sense of dedication, firm beliefs, humanistic qualities and great love.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
